Calamarain wrote:
> Boots of speed are a useful wish for anyone, they tend to be a priority
> for me.

If you can get basic intrinsic speed (archs have it), jumping boots are
vastly preferrable IMO _if_ you'll remember to use them.

> I would also use at least one of your wishes on a magic marker
> (if one has not appeared in the Mines or Minetown) - everyone always
> wants to write more scrolls.

Markers are a high priority once you have MR and reflection.  Getting
those (and PR) puts you in good position to ascend, so do that early
and save the other wishes.

> Another cool wish if you've found no artifacts yet is the Blessed +2
> Grayswandir. It's a very very nice weapon, and as a lawful - it's the
> best you're gonna get.

Best weapon in the game, but wishing for weapons is usually a waste
IMO.  Even if you wind up using a regular longsword and silver saber,
you'll be dealing out vast amounts of damage.  If you already have all
the necessities, though, may as well wish it up I guess.  I'd go for
MR, reflection, at least one marker, jumping, BoH, telecontrol, and a
lot of other stuff before Grayswandir, though.



